<<<
instead of the two, they, or nothing at all. The point is clear if the two sentences (a) Both fought well, & (b) To setile the matter both fought, are compared. In a, emphasis is wanted;
===
instead of *the two*, *they*, or nothing at all. The point is clear if the two sentences (a) *Both fought well*, & (b) *To settle the matter both fought*, are compared. In *a*, emphasis is wanted;
>>>

<<<
but, in b, of course one did not fight without the other’s fighting, since it takes two to make a fight; the needless both makes the reader wonder whom else they both fought.
===
but, in *b*, of course one did not fight without the other’s fighting, since it takes two to make a fight; the needless *both* makes the reader wonder whom else they both fought.
